WEBVTT

00:00:00.035 --> 00:00:03.390
Imagine the tracker owner believes an existing form saves

00:00:03.425 --> 00:00:04.191
submissions.

00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:08.115
If the agent designs a new database around that assumption

00:00:08.197 --> 00:00:11.784
without checking, the resulting plan may miss a system

00:00:11.935 --> 00:00:14.211
that already contains valuable information.

00:00:14.908 --> 00:00:18.692
A reality scan looks at the repository, documents, and the

00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:21.734
actual workflow the task permits the agent to inspect.

00:00:22.338 --> 00:00:25.426
Ask the agent to report what it examined and what it could

00:00:25.461 --> 00:00:26.251
not access.

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:29.316
The goal is to ground design in the current world.

00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:33.724
Create four columns: verified, planned, assumed, and

00:00:33.805 --> 00:00:34.328
unknown.

00:00:34.653 --> 00:00:38.380
"The repository contains a form component" may be verified

00:00:38.415 --> 00:00:39.065
from code.

00:00:39.274 --> 00:00:42.327
"The form currently receives live submissions" requires

00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:44.173
stronger evidence than code alone.

00:00:44.556 --> 00:00:46.147
A roadmap item is planned.

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:49.177
A belief that has not been checked is an assumption.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.207
If access is missing, call it unknown.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.725
A timestamp or revision helps another person know what the

00:00:55.794 --> 00:00:57.095
observation applies to.

00:00:57.698 --> 00:01:00.787
A clean-looking document does not magically turn a future

00:01:00.822 --> 00:01:02.145
goal into a live system.

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:05.767
For our fictional tracker, inspect the form, follow where

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.145
its data goes, and ask what happens after a user submits.

00:01:09.842 --> 00:01:11.827
Does it show an error if saving fails?

00:01:12.152 --> 00:01:13.697
Does anything send a message?

00:01:14.022 --> 00:01:16.251
Is there one record or several copies?

00:01:16.854 --> 00:01:19.920
A repository inspection might reveal that the form stores

00:01:20.001 --> 00:01:23.182
inquiries, while email import is only a proposal.

00:01:23.693 --> 00:01:26.712
Record the exact source of each claim and the limits of

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:27.594
the observation.

00:01:28.035 --> 00:01:31.344
We are not contacting actual organizers or sending real

00:01:31.402 --> 00:01:32.888
messages during the exercise.

00:01:33.181 --> 00:01:36.176
Suppose the team can either use the existing form only or

00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:37.546
add an email importer.

00:01:37.871 --> 00:01:41.668
Ask for each option's benefits, effort, dependencies,

00:01:41.946 --> 00:01:44.559
risks, and an explicit recommendation.

00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:48.146
The simplest choice may be to use the form first and defer

00:01:48.216 --> 00:01:48.645
import.

00:01:49.087 --> 00:01:51.455
That is not a promise never to build import.

00:01:51.896 --> 00:01:53.928
It gives the first version a bounded outcome.

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:57.318
Ask the owner questions that genuinely affect scope,

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:01.509
architecture, risk, or cost, instead of interrupting over

00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:02.914
every routine detail.

00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:06.951
A decision ledger records context, decision,

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:12.280
rationale, alternatives, consequences, status, and

00:02:12.327 --> 00:02:14.765
a condition that would justify reopening it.

00:02:15.148 --> 00:02:18.643
For example: "Provisionally use the website form for

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:22.300
version one, subject to confirming it exists and works.

00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:24.216
Defer email import.

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:27.594
Revisit when the owner has a tested export and approves

00:02:27.617 --> 00:02:31.692
the scope." Mark a choice as accepted, provisional,

00:02:31.867 --> 00:02:33.318
deferred, or rejected.

00:02:33.759 --> 00:02:37.822
If a decision changes later, add a dated supersession note

00:02:38.031 --> 00:02:41.027
rather than silently pretending the old decision never

00:02:41.096 --> 00:02:41.677
existed.

00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:45.104
Before architecture, review the facts that materially

00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:46.196
affect the design.

00:02:46.637 --> 00:02:47.786
Which are verified?

00:02:48.065 --> 00:02:50.004
Which can be safely assumed for planning?

00:02:50.445 --> 00:02:51.792
Which require a decision?

00:02:52.233 --> 00:02:55.368
If you cannot access the live form, you can design around

00:02:55.402 --> 00:02:58.874
a clearly labeled assumption, but you must not claim its

00:02:58.967 --> 00:03:00.407
live behavior is proven.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:04.087
A useful research report ends with the exact evidence

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:08.533
found, contradictions, recommended options, and the

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.170
decisions that remain with the owner.

00:03:10.487 --> 00:03:13.842
For the tracker, a responsible investigator might open the

00:03:13.889 --> 00:03:16.698
form source, identify the handler that receives

00:03:16.721 --> 00:03:19.519
submissions, and inspect any existing test.

00:03:19.903 --> 00:03:23.246
The result could be: "A form component exists at this

00:03:23.327 --> 00:03:27.507
revision; a local test covers required fields." That does

00:03:27.577 --> 00:03:30.247
not prove the deployed site uses the same revision.

00:03:30.572 --> 00:03:34.148
If deployment information is unavailable, record that gap.

00:03:34.473 --> 00:03:38.409
A screenshot, a source file, a test result, and a live

00:03:38.455 --> 00:03:40.382
observation support different claims.

00:03:40.823 --> 00:03:43.517
The reader should never have to guess which one was used.

00:03:43.875 --> 00:03:46.778
"Research everything" is expensive and hard to verify.

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:50.922
Ask targeted questions: Where does the form send data?

00:03:51.526 --> 00:03:53.604
Where is the authoritative inquiry record?

00:03:54.046 --> 00:03:55.903
What happens when saving fails?

00:03:56.228 --> 00:03:58.631
Is email import actually implemented?

00:03:59.235 --> 00:04:02.266
The agent can inspect the relevant files and summarize

00:04:02.289 --> 00:04:03.462
with paths and evidence.

00:04:03.903 --> 00:04:06.968
If it cannot access a necessary system, it should state

00:04:07.003 --> 00:04:08.268
the exact limitation.

00:04:08.651 --> 00:04:11.194
This keeps the research proportional to the decision at

00:04:11.252 --> 00:04:14.537
hand and avoids drowning the owner in unrelated detail.

00:04:14.853 --> 00:04:17.059
Suppose option one uses the form only.

00:04:17.442 --> 00:04:20.566
It is narrower and avoids an email integration, but the

00:04:20.647 --> 00:04:22.922
owner must handle email inquiries separately.

00:04:23.364 --> 00:04:25.546
Option two adds an email importer.

00:04:25.929 --> 00:04:30.225
It may reduce manual work, but requires access, a matching

00:04:30.283 --> 00:04:33.487
strategy, privacy decisions, and failure handling.

00:04:34.091 --> 00:04:36.808
A decision is easier when each option includes both

00:04:36.866 --> 00:04:38.224
benefits and costs.

00:04:38.665 --> 00:04:41.092
A recommendation should say why it fits the current

00:04:41.126 --> 00:04:44.215
outcome, not simply claim that one approach is best for

00:04:44.273 --> 00:04:44.749
everyone.

00:04:45.065 --> 00:04:47.445
Some decisions can be made using ordinary project

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:48.165
conventions.

00:04:48.606 --> 00:04:51.555
Others change what the product does or what access it

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:52.124
needs.

00:04:52.565 --> 00:04:55.235
The owner should decide whether the first release imports

00:04:55.282 --> 00:04:58.846
an inbox, sends messages, or handles real customer

00:04:58.892 --> 00:04:59.566
information.

00:05:00.169 --> 00:05:03.165
The agent can recommend a safe default and do independent

00:05:03.211 --> 00:05:04.697
work while the answer is pending.

00:05:05.301 --> 00:05:08.842
Ask only the question that changes the design: "Should the

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.652
first version include email import, or should it track

00:05:11.733 --> 00:05:13.254
form submissions only?"

00:05:13.564 --> 00:05:18.394
A useful ledger entry has a title, date, context, accepted

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.132
choice, alternatives considered, rationale,

00:05:22.573 --> 00:05:25.151
consequences, and an explicit status.

00:05:25.661 --> 00:05:29.226
A reopen condition might be "the owner approves inbox

00:05:29.307 --> 00:05:32.581
access and supplies representative synthetic export

00:05:32.615 --> 00:05:36.807
examples." If a later decision replaces it, preserve the

00:05:36.899 --> 00:05:39.047
earlier entry and link the new decision.

00:05:39.651 --> 00:05:42.797
This history is useful because future contributors can

00:05:42.867 --> 00:05:45.897
understand both what was chosen and why a seemingly

00:05:45.967 --> 00:05:47.813
attractive alternative was deferred.

00:05:48.121 --> 00:05:50.083
New evidence can overturn an assumption.

00:05:50.466 --> 00:05:53.496
Suppose a live inspection shows that the old form does not

00:05:53.555 --> 00:05:54.913
save inquiries at all.

00:05:55.517 --> 00:05:58.918
Record the new observation, revise the dependency in the

00:05:58.965 --> 00:06:02.088
architecture, and tell the owner whether the scope or

00:06:02.157 --> 00:06:03.388
timeline changes.

00:06:03.771 --> 00:06:06.813
The decision ledger is not a rule against learning; it

00:06:06.859 --> 00:06:09.762
prevents silent changes and needless repetition.

00:06:10.366 --> 00:06:13.013
An agent should correct stale statements when it has

00:06:13.094 --> 00:06:15.904
evidence and clearly identify which claims remain

00:06:15.973 --> 00:06:16.740
unverified.

00:06:17.031 --> 00:06:20.096
If an important fact cannot be verified, write the

00:06:20.189 --> 00:06:22.905
uncertainty next to the decision it affects.

00:06:23.347 --> 00:06:27.259
For example, the team may provisionally design a form-only

00:06:27.317 --> 00:06:30.417
workflow while awaiting access to the existing form.

00:06:31.114 --> 00:06:34.411
State the assumption, who can resolve it, and what would

00:06:34.458 --> 00:06:35.979
change if it proves false.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:39.775
A provisional decision lets independent thinking continue

00:06:39.798 --> 00:06:42.306
without pretending the question is closed.

00:06:42.689 --> 00:06:45.835
When evidence arrives, compare it to the assumption and

00:06:45.893 --> 00:06:48.749
either confirm the decision or record a dated change.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:51.721
This approach is particularly valuable when an owner or

00:06:51.814 --> 00:06:54.485
outside provider cannot respond immediately.
